				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Too hot. Reyia reached up and brushed the hair back from her face, feeling the sweat on her brow smear her silk sleeve as she did so. This was her first trip to the desert of Northern Ro, and she was not accustomed to the heat. She had been in the Eastern commonlands hunting Deathfist orcs when her neighbor Duroz had suggested they travel to the desert to test their steel and courage upon Dervish bandits. Soon after she had met Duroz and his band near a camp in North Ro. Now they sat a few paces away and planned the attack. There were six of them, and only three dervish cutthroats, but it still was wise to plan ahead, as they wished no deaths or serious injury, and besides, there could always be more dervs lurking about. 
<br />

<br />
   Now it was time. With a mighty shout the warriors charged into the camp and began battle. Reyia stood a few paces off and began to cast spells to cripple the Derv's fighting power and increase her own band's effectiveness. Her hands glowed and pulsed with magical energy and her brow began to sweat as she fought to increase the power of spells. Her band had overestimated the power of the Dervs...and as two more joined in the fight, her band began to retreat backwards. But there was nowhere to run to....the Dervs howled in victory as they cut down each member of the party one by one...Reyia stood in horror as her friend Duroz was impaled by three swords and then tossed away. Her closest friend...the one who stood in Neriak with her for hours as she dreamed of getting away...of escaping her father, who never seemed to approve of her no matter how hard she worked.
<br />

<br />
   The with a start she realized that her entire party had been slain...and four Dervs were advancing on her grinning from ear to ear. She had no where to run...and no one was there to help her. She thought of tossing up a prayer to Innorouk &lt;sp?&gt; but she had long since discovered he was not a god of mercy. Then she clumsily tripped over one of her sandals and fell in the sand. She felt a hand reach towards her back...and then she heard yelling. Sounds of battle surrounded her....and she couldn't understand why the cutthroats had yet to kill her too. Then, all of a sudden...silence. And she heard a sound...it was of heavy plate boots hitting metal. 
<br />

<br />
      She raised an eye and then almost gasped. Standing above her was the most beautiful sight she had ever seen. For many years afterwards she never forgot the first time she saw Antilles Wolfkin. His armor gleamed in the hot sun...but his eyes, a deep bright blue, regarded her solemnly...almost with pity. &quot;Are you alright, lass?&quot; he spoke. His voice was deep, hearty, and rugged, and she felt a strange flutter go through her body. She stared up at him, unable to speak. Antilles tried again &quot;Can you walk? There may be more Dervs coming any time. We must travel to Freeport.&quot; The mention of the city kindled some sense back in Reyia and she scrambled to her feet, only to exclaim in pain and shock and crumple. Reyia blinked back tears &quot;My ankle...I don't think I can walk....&quot; Antilles nodded. &quot;I shall have to carry you then.&quot;  And with one deft move he seized the Tier Dal up in his arms and began running off. It was only at the exact moment that Reyia realized it was one of the Fier Dal who had saved her. She had been brought up her entire life to believe that they, and the Koala Dal hated her and her kind, and would kill any that they had the moment to kill. Immediately she shifted and her thoughts scattered. She felt his heart beat as he ran....as he ran away to save her. To keep her safe. He cared about her safety. Perhaps he was different? Or perhaps not all she had been told were true? She was too tired to think...she relaxed and enjoyed the feeling of being in the arms of the most magnificient male she had ever met. 
<br />

<br />
To be continued.....
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Jesent Wolfkin
<br />

<br />
Warrior of the Concordat 
