				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Months later.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia leaned forward over the body of a young Koala Dal woman that had wandered a bit too far from the safety of Felwithe a bit too soon. Noting the little the woman carried on her, Reyia snorted and quickly hid herself. She closed her eyes and began meditating, feeling her exhausted mana reflow into her pores. As she sat, she mentally ran through what the day held. Several dead elves, a minimum of experience and loot. She had grown too strong, too quickly. There was very little she could find that was any challenge to her and her growing abilities. After a moment she regained her strength and began stealthfully creeping forward once more near Felwithe, looking for another elf over confident in themself. Seeing a pair of young mages leave the gate and move away from the protection of the guards, she grinned. It was always more fun with two. A quick spell, and one would murder the other, and then a couple more spells and the other would be dead as well. It was always fun seeing the horror in their eyes as they killed people they loved. Reyia felt a shiver run up her legs and tried to calm herself. 
<br />

<br />
     &quot;He is coming soon, says my mother.&quot; One elf spoke to the other and Reyia leaned forward to listen. She had quickly learned, in the months she had been on Faydwer alone, that information was the strongest ally of a Tier Dal in these parts where many, if not most, wished her dead. The other elf replied &quot;Antilles? It has been a long time since he visited Kelethin. They say he brings the most marvelous gifts for the young adventurers in training. I will surely be there.&quot; Reyia felt her blood run cold. Antilles. She bit her lip and closed her eyes, his final words to her running through her mind. She clenched her fists, attempting to slow the rush of the memories....&quot;...I just don't love you that way. Not the way you love me.&quot;
<br />

<br />
        The two mages forgotten, Reyia sank to the ground closing her eyes and shifting back and forth, trying to hold back tears. She did not even notice the two elves begin running to Kelethin. One last statement reached her ears before they disappeared out of view &quot;He will be there in a four days, says mother.&quot; Reyia's mind whirled. Four days. What should she do? She knew that she should keep away from him and Kelethin. The plan she had told Antilles of before he left her would be impossible now, she had killed far too many elves testing their strength to gain the trust of the two towns. She bit her lip again and brushed back her hair out of her eyes. I have to see him, she thought. I have four days to figure out how. That is enough time. I will see him. Then a thought exploded in her mind! Of course! How silly she was not to think of it right away! She was an enchantress, she could cast illusions. She could easily change her body to that of a wood elf and meet Antilles. Perhaps she would even be able to touch his hand. Her cheeks turned from a light bluish color to almost marr cherry red. Soon she thought...soon...I will see the man I love again.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
To be continued yet again....
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Jesent Wolfkin
<br />

<br />
Warrior of the Concordat
