			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Reyia twisted the silk scarf around her and strained her eyes over the crowd. Antilles was said to be just forward with several bags of gifts he was giving out, although she hadn't yet seen him. There were too many youngsters pushing past her trying to see what wonders the old warrior had brought them from lands they had only dreamed of. Then at last the youngsters began leaving, to use their new weapons or show their new clothing or armor to their friends who had been unable to escape chores or lessons. Finally Reyia was alone with Antilles. She shivered slightly, knowing that although her illusion of a wood elf changed her appearance enough as to make her appear a completely different person. She had seen a young girl out in the woods just hours before gathering fruit and vegetables for her family and had taken her prisoner with barely a struggle. Even now, Villiosious, her gnome wizard friend, had her bound and watched near a dark part of the Faydark no one visited. Reyia had easily taken the form of the girl and returned to the village, where no one yet had seen through her illusion. Antilles looked at the girl in front of him and smiled. &quot;Well now child,  I think I have something for you too. What skills do you wish to develop? Do you desire a finely crafted blade or would a piece of jewelry which increases your wisdom serve you better?&quot; Reyia shifted slightly and tried to disguise her voice. &quot;None, m'lord, I am but a simple girl, and I do not wish to take up fighting. I just lost my parents recently to an attack of the Crushbone orcs and am kind of at a loose end. I saw the crowd over here and was merely curious as to what the excitement was about.&quot; Antilles nodded somberly at the girl &quot;Many of us have lost loved ones to those vile creatures. I wish I could bring back your parents, child. If you need a place to stay, then my house here has several empty rooms. I am not often there, as many call for my help throughout the world, but you are welcome to stay there if you need a place.&quot; Reyia smiled secretly to herself. &quot;M'lord, that is too generous of you. I don't know how I will ever be able to repay you.&quot; Antilles looked uncomfortable &quot;It is but a small thing. I am happy only if I can help you in some way. Come now, child, I will show you where it is.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Jesent Wolfkin
<br />

<br />
son of Antilles 
<br />
<i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
