			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Reyia was screaming. Antilles woke up quickly and moved from his room and hurried down the hall to her room. Norrath was a dangerous world, and there was no telling what manner of beast might be attacking her. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia was sleeping in her bed, tossing around, and tearing at her blankets and pillow. Her screams should surely be audible even several homes away. She was twelve again, and outside from Neriak in the Nektulos forest gathering herbs for her mother to make dinner with. Her father had warned her to be quick about it, and her back still burned from earlier today when she had been too slow performing a chore. She was hurrying so quickly that she didn't see an undead skeleton make its way towards her. Until she felt a cold clammy hand slap her against her back. Rolling over, she quickly got to her feet and watched it approach her with horror. Immediately she took off running praying that a guard would find her before the skeleton caught her. Just as the skeleton closed in, she caught a glimpse of a Tier Dal man in shimmering plate armor. She yelled out for help, and he began running towards her. The guard quickly tossed her aside and engaged the skeleton in combat. With a mighty swipe of his fine steel sword, the skeleton crumpled to the ground, a pile of bone chips once more. The guard turned to her &quot;Be more careful child.&quot; Instantly the guard caught sight of a Fier Dal man in blazing red armor moving through the forest. &quot;He dares to intrude upon sacred ground?&quot; growled the guard and he ran off towards the man. Reyia sat there, still partly in shock at her close call, and watched the two engage in combat. Suddenly she realized the guard was losing. The wood elf swung his blade around and magic shimmered off of it, causing the guard to flinch openly each time the weapon swung. The guard was forced backwards, and Reyia realized with dismay he would soon be upon her. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
She rose up and tried to move but just then the Tier Dal stumbled into her. Both men looked shocked that the girl was there, and Reyia felt again the pain course through her as the poison on the wood elf's blade infected her. She screamed again as she fell on the ground, her body convulsing in agony. She looked up at the wood elf's face and screamed again. Antilles. Antilles was fighting the guard.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Antilles pounded on her bedroom door. &quot;Child? Are you alright?&quot; Reyia realized with horror her wood elf illusion had worn off. &quot;Yes, yes,  I am fine.&quot; She quickly rose her hands and wrapped herself with magic again and spoke &quot;I'm sorry. You can come in.&quot; Antilles swung open the door and looked around. &quot;Child? What happened? I feared you had been attacked.&quot; Reyia looked sheepish. &quot;I am sorry sir. It was but a dream.&quot; Remembering it again, she sank on the bed. Antilles quickly moved to the bed and caught her before she collapsed. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia looked up again into the beautiful blue eyes that were looking right into her own. She shivered. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Antilles spoke &quot;M'lady, are you cold?&quot; Reyia shook her head, unable to speak. She brushed her hands over his bulging muscles in his arm and shivered again. Antilles lowered his head, closer and closer to hers, until just a fraction of an inch seperated their lips. He hesitated, but Reyia rose her lips up, kissing Antilles deeply. It was several minutes before she lowered herself again, sighing in contentment. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Antilles looked a little befuddled. Reyia smiled inwardly, knowing that although the warrior was very knowledgable about many types of fighting, in the manner of romance he was very inexperienced. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Antilles cleared his throat. &quot;What is your name?&quot; Reyia rose her head and looked into his eyes. &quot;Reyia&quot; she said without thinking.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Antilles almost dropped her. &quot;Reyia?&quot; he asked. Reyia swore inwardly and nodded. &quot;Why do you look so surprised, m'lord?&quot; Antilles looked up at the ceiling. &quot;My apologies. I once knew another with that name.&quot; Reyia sighed in relief. &quot;Were you close, m'lord?&quot; Antilles looked away again. &quot;I suppose...we were. She wanted more from me than I could give her....and we went seperate ways.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia tried to look surprised. &quot;That is very strange, Antilles. Now...will you kiss me again?&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Five months later, they were married.  
<br />
