			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9098&amp;sid=3e4b5a2a03e170ff17f00e7370b40c1c#9098"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Fri Apr 05, 2002 3:59 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9098&amp;sid=3e4b5a2a03e170ff17f00e7370b40c1c"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">It was her wedding night, and the happiest night of Reyia Wolfkin's life. She lay next to her husband, who at this very moment was trying to ward away evil with a mighty snore, and she giggled slightly to herself. She stopped herself mid giggle, wondering how long it had been since her heart had felt so light. Instantly, memories rushed into her head, and her good mood evaporated. Antilles had struck her with his sword. The disease she was infected with had never fully disappeared, and since that day, her time of the month had come irregularly, sometimes with a eight or ten month interval, sometimes once a week, and always with frightful pain. She remembered traveling with Duroz in North Karana and encountering a pack of gypsies, who had told her fortune. She could still hear the words of the young beautiful woman....
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Someone has hurt you child. I sense that in years to come he will become important to you. You will hurt him, and heal him, and hurt him again.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
At her words, Reyia shaked her head in confusion. The gypsy continued on...
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Child...the injury you carry...it has affected your ability to give birth. ONE time, and only one, will you become pregnant. This child will be your only hope of giving to your husband the young he desires.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia had become numb with fear and despair, and had paid a few silver to the woman quietly before leaving with her neighbor. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia flashed back to the present. Oh Innoruuk she thought, grim with realization that if the god was listening, he likely did not care, or even desired her harm, Antilles wants children. I have seen the way he is with the young ones in the village. And I have but one chance to give him what he desires.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Months went by. Reyia realized that her belly had started growing larger, and she was ill early in the morning. She held out til there could be no doubt. She was pregnant. She wondered if Antilles suspected. She was slim by nature, and the differences in his body would require a subtle eye to detect. Normally, Antilles was very observant by nature, but she had taken specific cares in her married life to avoid detection. She spent most of her time by herself, and always arose several times a night to renew her illusion of a wood elf, in case it had dropped while she was sleeping. Inside she knew that this was a foolhardy plan. She couldn't last forever with these tricks. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
But her mind desperately told her that if she could give Antilles the son he wanted, then he would never cast her away from him. Their love would continue to grow strong and secure. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Then one night, Antilles was away from home in service to his guild. She tossed and turned in bed, afraid for his safety. He had been to the Plane of Fear before, and had always returned, but the minions of Cazic Thule were certantly not to be taken lightly. She at last rose from bed, knowing that she would not soon be able to sleep, and wrapped a fur lined cloak around her growing body, and walked through Kelethin. She walked around the platforms high in the air. It was late, and mostly empty, but a few people were traveling around, and most of the taverns still had a few people inside. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
It was just outside one of those taverns when her body began to tremble again. Aftershocks of the disease she thought, and laid down on the ground trying not to panic. She wrapped her arms around her swollen belly and tried to hold back tears that threatened to spill from her eyes. She lay there long, fighting the pain, that finally, from exhaustion, she fell asleep.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Drin Stonebreaker and Mart Hollowskin left the inside of a tavern in Kelethin. Their failures in fighting inside Crushbone earlier in the day had made them both indulge in the numbing power of alcohol...and their eyes were glazed from a few too many mugs of the brew. It was then they came upon Reyia.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Her wood elf illusion had fallen.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Whass diss?&quot; slurred Drin to Mart. &quot;why one of dose steenkin darkeez bee up here?&quot; &quot;Less teach her a lessun&quot; agreed Mart. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia was dragged awake by rough hands on her arms. She screamed out loud in surprise and fear and watched two Fier Dal men staring at her coldly. They asked what she thought she was doing there, and she tried to stumble out an apology, but they wouldn't let her talk. The hands picked her up and carried her to the edge of the platform. Reyia closed her eyes desperately. Please she thought. Please send help. Not even sure who she was praying to...then she felt herself falling. She closed her eyes and thought...everything will be alright. Someone will help. Please let everything be alright....
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Then her body hit the ground hard. Blood rushed out from her, broken in several places. But the fall hadn't killed her. And her last conscious thoughts before blanking out were....
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Everything will be alright. The baby will be fine. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
But tears were pouring down her cheeks. She no longer believed the words. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Jesent Wolfkin, son of Antilles. 
<br />

<br />
Warrior of the Concordat 
<br />
