		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9113&amp;sid=3e4b5a2a03e170ff17f00e7370b40c1c#9113"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Fri May 17, 2002 4:43 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9113&amp;sid=3e4b5a2a03e170ff17f00e7370b40c1c"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">A gnome, training in battle against the Crushbone orcs in the Greater Faydark found Reyia a few hours later. Although he had taken up the trade of a wizard, he bandaged her wounds as best as he could, then wisely had not taken her to Kelethin or Felwithe to be healed, but instead into Ak'anon to the clerics who resided there. Reyia's broken bones were mended, and her bruises and gashes were healed. In the three months she was there, she didn't speak a word to anyone. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
When Antilles discovered her missing, he went out into the world to search her out, but his description of a Fier Dal maiden didn't match Reyia's true self. After having stayed in the cleric guild until her strength returned, she sought out the wizard who had saved her. She spoke for the first time to him, asking his name, and then begging him to teleport her near Neriak. The gnome, unable to say no to her, teleported her there. In the years to come, the two would become close friends. But this day, he quickly said goodbye to Reyia as she returned home to her father. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia was beaten mercilessly by her father, who was not at all pleased she had disappeared for so long, nor at her even returning to his home. Her father called her a fool, and suggested that she spend some time with her much younger brother, though he was far behind her in age, at least he knew how to serve Innoruuk and his family. Reyia bit her tongue, and sent for the wood elf maiden she had imprisoned months ago. She went deep into the depths of Neriak and sought out an unlikely pair of Tier Dal....one a necromancer, foul and decaying under his splendid purple robe, the other a tall and strikingly beautiful cleric girl. The two took the wood elf maiden, and Reyia, and over several weeks, experimented with their faces, and at last reached the point where, under wood elf illusion, no one could tell the two apart. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reyia then returned to Faydwer, and took up residence in the mysterious forest of Lesser Faydark. She sent the wood elf girl, after threatening the lives of her family, and hers, to Antilles, to bear him the children he wanted. She did so, giving birth to two strong sons, only a year apart, and then a half dozen years later, to another son. The last son, on the day he was born, reached out to his father, and clutched his hand with his own, and refused to let go. Antilles was deeply affected by the simple gesture of the infant, and he quickly became his father's favorite. Years later, Jesent Wolfkin, Antilles's third son, would become a member of the Concordat Angelis. But that is a story for another time.  
<br />
<i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
